---
description: Continue approved bounded work through completion without repeated micro-approvals
alwaysApply: true
---

# Continue Through Bounded Work

- At the start of a multi-step task, consolidate the required decisions,
  assumptions, approval gates, deliverables, and verification evidence into
  one concise approval set.
- Once Carl approves that set, continue through all routine, reversible,
  read-only, implementation, testing, documentation, and coordination steps
  that remain inside the approved scope. Do not pause for approval after every
  tiny task or intermediate success.
- Maintain an active goal for substantial work and keep moving across turns
  until the goal's completion evidence is satisfied. Give concise progress
  updates and state the next gate rather than reopening settled decisions.
- Stop and ask Carl plainly when a genuinely new product, security, scope,
  credential, destructive-action, external-state, or policy decision appears;
  when an approval no longer covers the proposed action; or when a blocker
  cannot be resolved safely with in-scope evidence and alternatives.
- Never treat this rule as blanket permission for production mutations,
  irreversible deletion, migrations, invitations, credential changes, or
  unrelated work. Preserve explicit target, rollback, observation, audit, and
  verification gates.
- For parallel-agent work, keep the coordination board current, avoid overlap,
  and surface genuine Carl-decision items in the conversation as well as in
  the board. Routine no-decision coordination updates may remain board-only.
